<LanguageData>
  
  <!-- EN: Pileus Hat -->
  <BA_PileusHat.label>皮莱乌斯帽</BA_PileusHat.label>
  <!-- EN: The pileus was a brimless felt cap worn in Ancient Greece, Etruria, Illyria later also introduced in Ancient Rome. In various artistic depictions in the middle Byzantine period soldiers are seen wearing pilos caps.\n\n<i><color=#66E0E4FF>Medieval Kingdoms: Byzantine Empire</color></i> -->
  <BA_PileusHat.description>皮莱乌斯帽是古希腊、伊特鲁里亚及伊利里亚地区流行的无檐毡帽，后传入古罗马。在中拜占庭时期的各类艺术作品中，可见士兵佩戴此类帽子的形象。</BA_PileusHat.description>
  
</LanguageData>